We own this fork. Edits are normal code changes; we do not track upstream
automatically. To pull a specific upstream change later, cherry-pick from a
local clone of openai/codex into vendor/codex-rs/.

Awidat workspace lints (unwrap_used=deny, etc.) are scoped to crates/* and
do not apply here.

Our edits (re-apply after every refresh):
- vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/cli.rs: `#[derive(Parser, Debug, Default)]` on `Cli`
  so awidat-cli can construct one programmatically. See crates/cli/src/chat_codex_cmd.rs.
- vendor/codex-rs/login/src/auth/default_client.rs,
  vendor/codex-rs/models-manager/src/lib.rs,
  vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/lib.rs, and
  vendor/codex-rs/exec/src/event_processor_with_human_output.rs:
  stamp Codex client version as "0.128.0" instead of Awidat's inherited
  CARGO_PKG_VERSION ("0.1.0"). The working installed CLI sends
  `Codex Desktop/0.128.0 ... (codex_exec; 0.128.0)` and
  `/codex/models?client_version=0.128.0`; sending `0.1.0` in the suffix
  or models query trips OpenAI's newer-model gate with "requires a newer
  version of Codex". Bump these stamps when intentionally matching a newer
  installed/published Codex CLI.
- vendor/codex-rs/core/src/client.rs and vendor/codex-rs/core/src/turn_metadata.rs:
  omit newer websocket client metadata that the installed 0.128.0 CLI does not
  send (`x-codex-ws-stream-request-start-ms` and `thread_id` inside
  `x-codex-turn-metadata`). The server applies the same newer-model gate to
  this request surface, even when User-Agent and auth match.
- vendor/codex-rs/analytics/src/events.rs:
  stamp analytics `runtime.codex_rs_version` as "0.128.0"; the installed CLI
  sends this value before the model request, while the fork's inherited "0.1.0"
  remains another visible stale-version signal.
- vendor/codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs and
  vendor/codex-rs/codex-api/src/requests/headers.rs:
  match the installed Responses WebSocket HTTP header surface. The important
  gate signal was the provider `version` header, which still said "0.1.0" even
  after the User-Agent was fixed. The installed CLI sends `version: 0.128.0`,
  `session_id`, and no `thread-id` header.
- vendor/codex-rs/Cargo.toml + Cargo.lock: deleted. The codex crates live
  inside Awidat's single root workspace.
